/* ══ CATALOGUE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   The markup here used to be a search-and-filter "explorer": a rail, a search
   box and a results pane. None of it was ever styled and no script was ever
   written, so in the browser it was an 7,789px column of unstyled list items
   with a white search field sitting on a dark page. Twenty-one services in
   four groups are perfectly scannable without any of that, so this is a plain
   catalogue: jump links, four groups, a card per service carrying the two
   facts a visitor is actually choosing on — what it starts from and how long
   it takes. No JavaScript, nothing to go stale. */

.sx-jump {
